cvars.helptext:
How the map author is shown on the automap.
// 0 - Off
// 1 - Static
// 2 - Fade in/out with map name
// 3 - Marquee in/out with map name
// 4 - Teletype effect with map name

Default netdemo name.  Parses the following tokens:
// %d: date in YYYYMMDD format
// %t: time in HHMMSS format
// %n: player name
// %g: gametype
// %w: WAD file loaded; either the first PWAD or the IWAD
// %m: Map lump
// %%: Literal percent sign

Move floors and ceilings immediately instead of waiting for confirmation, values are:
// 0 - Don't predict any sectors
// 1 - Predict all sectors based only on actor movements
// 2 - Predict only sectors activated by you

Default screenshot name.  Parses the following tokens:
// %d: date in YYYYMMDD format
// %t: time in HHMMSS format
// %n: player name
// %g: gametype
// %w: WAD file loaded; either the first PWAD or the IWAD
// %m: Map lump
// %%: Literal percent sign

Name of the actor type to spawn as a helper.
// Spawnable actors can be found using the ccmd `dumpactors`
// If empty, it uses the defined default friend in Dehacked (BEX).
// If the actor name can't be found, an MBF helper dog will be spawned

Use MBF player_helpers behavior -- amount of friendly things to spawn at map start.
// If in an online game, dogs spawn only once on map start per helper per player.
// The helper type is defined in BEX or through the cvar co_friend_helpertype.

Removes some things from the map. Values are:
// -1 - Multiplayer things are added in singleplayer.
// 0 - All things are retained (default).
// 1 - Only Coop weapons are removed.
// 2 - All Coop things are removed.
// 3 - All pickupable things are removed.

Show kills, items, and secrets:
// 0: Off
// 1: DIGFONT
// 2: SMALLFONT
// 3: DIGFONT, vertical arrangement
// 4: SMALLFONT, vertical arrangement

Show the HUD timer:
// 0: No Timer
// 1: Count-down Timer
// 2: Count-up timer

Sets the behavior of on-screen prompts of when to name gamepad buttons instead of keyboard keys.
// 0 - Follow whichever device was used last
// 1 - Mouse input does not switch away from the gamepad
// 2 - Always show gamepad keys

Sets the game mode, values are:
// 0 = Cooperative
// 1 = Deathmatch
// 2 = Team Deathmatch
// 3 = Capture The Flag
// 4 = Horde

Sets the skill level, values are:
// 0 - No things mode
// 1 - I'm Too Young To Die
// 2 - Hey, Not Too Rough
// 3 - Hurt Me Plenty
// 4 - Ultra-Violence
// 5 - Nightmare
